Cell["\<\
The bond direction is Normalize[finalPoint-initialPoint]. Supply distinct \
three-component points. No radial dependence or distance cutoff is applied to \
the supplied integrals.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->550127710,ExpressionUUID->"21bead47-b7db-ae4a-b033-39f719ce989f"],

Cell["\<\
Orbital order is {s, px, py, pz, dxy, dyz, dzx, dx2-y2, d3z2-r2}, omitting \
the d orbitals for \"sp\".\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1414230100,ExpressionUUID->"3266edf3-c600-914e-a160-6f8bc3bac9e2"],

Cell["\<\
The 10-parameter spd form uses \
{ssSigma,spSigma,sdSigma,ppSigma,ppPi,pdSigma,pdPi,ddSigma,ddPi,ddDelta}; \
reverse-shell parameters are identified with their forward counterparts.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1527771242,ExpressionUUID->"c84f4fa7-aba8-9b46-b03e-75f8d50ddc7b"],

Cell["\<\
The 14-parameter spd form uses \
{ssSigma,spSigma,sdSigma,psSigma,ppSigma,ppPi,pdSigma,pdPi,dsSigma,dpSigma,\
dpPi,ddSigma,ddPi,ddDelta}.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1659023560,ExpressionUUID->"fd8e2adf-0c38-954b-b981-994ecffa6e2e"],

Cell["\<\
Reverse-shell signs use ordinary transpose: p-to-s and d-to-p are negated, \
while d-to-s is not. For complex integrals, ensure the opposite directed bond \
is supplied consistently.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->988687487,ExpressionUUID->"e72da35a-1d55-8945-bb28-2d149ecb10d7"]
}, Closed]],

